rs the approved scope for after convergence. No hosted CI has run on this head yet (hostedCi: []).","name":"evidence","outcome":"FAIL"},{"evidence":"Changed paths are limited to the new sweep-records module and its mirror, round-policy, review-findings, small edits in execution.js and boundary-review.js, docs, the help text, the inventory and projection manifest, and tests. That matches plan steps P1-P6 and the mandate's limits on execution.js and boundary-review.js. Planning reviews and metrics are unchanged (D7). The feature base was moved to the merge base after merging main (S13), so the diff holds only this feature.","name":"scope","outcome":"PASS"},{"evidence":"There are two blocking medium findings, CR5-1 (code) and EV5-1 (evidence). Both are on packet.roundPolicy.regressionPaths (execution.js; cli/test/self-validation.test.js and review-packet.test.js), so they block under the round-5 band. No earlier dispositions are required (dispositionsRequired is empty). The history gaps (14 unavailable prior results) were handled by doing a fresh full assessment; earlier claims such as the Codex round-2 PASS and the CR-2 low finding are implementer records and were not relied on.","name":"findings","outcome":"FAIL"}],"dispositions":[],"featureId":"tb-convergence-sweep-records","findingProvenance":[{"id":"claude-code/CR5-1","model":"claude-opus-5-5","originalId":"CR5-1","provider":"claude-code"},{"id":"claude-code/EV5-1","model":"claude-opus-5-5","originalId":"EV5-1","provider":"claude-code"}],"findings":[{"blocking":true,"classId":"reintroduction-origin-lost","classStatement":"When a re-report reopens a closed finding, its earlier closures are cleared from the next round's history, so qualification attributes a reintroduced finding to its first raise instead of the reintroducing round.","criterion":"gate:review","evidence":"execution.js:1035-1037: `if (known) Object.assign(known, { open: true, closure: null, closures: [], reopened: ref })` keeps ref = the first raising